HISTORICAL first local-contact candidate, preceding final lifecycle fixes.
The qualified successor is integrated in AcustraEngine; do not apply this patch
on top of current source. This artifact reconstructs the first scored candidate.
Base commit: b958979497a17c869839a50b80d8069f87fedab1
Only ordinary steel contact bursts change. No contact amplitude fitting.
The existing displacement-noise signal is phenomenological, not a measured force.
For p=x/L and D=2L/c, incident contact = g/sqrt(2) * [e(t-pD/2)-e(t-(1-p/2)D)].
g=.76 vertical/.51 horizontal; old boundary writes are removed for these voices.
Fixed allpass delays preserve each directional wave's derivative-energy norm.
This preserves EMITTED source energy, not total stored energy or microphone RMS:
coherent force work with existing waves and the coupled bridge still needs audit.
First-arrival dispersion/loss is not modeled; existing losses apply on subsequent
round trips. Delay paths freeze at note-on, ignoring changes during the few-ms
contact. Repluck/clearDelay discard pending contact history; this is not a
qualified contact model for refrets/release/rapid retrigger. Those gates remain.
Fractional Thiran phase is approximate, especially near Nyquist/at8k; rate gates
and fixed-window attack spectra are required before any integration.
See Docs/contact-travel-2026-09-08.md for final qualification and limitations.

